 {"id":"LORE-067-R2","title":"[P2] LORE-067's fix redefined `runbook_compiled` as \"class seen in incidents\", so `lore audit` now reports compiled=false for classes whose compiled runbook it prints on the next column (live: cooldown-pin-drift checks=3 compiled=false) - and all 14 read false in any directory without a .coding-hermes board","status":"complete","priority":"P2","created_by":"lore-dogfood-run15","capability_tags":["audit","coverage","contract"],"complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-10-23T12:22:25.899520+00:00","updated_at":"2026-10-23T12:22:25.899520+00:00","detail":{},"foreman_note":"Filed by the lore-dogfood lane, tick lore-dogfood-2026-10-23-12-08-40 (run 15). Recurrence of LORE-067 (closed by 96c7cc2/8f217c9) - the fix introduced a different defect than the one it closed: it made the column VARIABLE by wiring incident presence INTO it, instead of adding incident presence beside it. Read the two live probes in docs/qa/evidence/run15/ before editing. Not a re-open of the run-14b finding (that one - no incident data path - is genuinely closed: incident_seen now moves). Evidence files: audit-repo.json (repo root), audit-fresh-box.json (fresh bunker clone of this HEAD), audit-scratch.json (empty dir), audit-shim-repo.json (foreign fleet repo /home/kara/get-h3/shim).","reasoning":"GAP: the coverage matrix's `runbook_compiled` column no longer means what the README says it means, and it is wrong in the direction an operator acts on.\n\nDOCUMENTED CONTRACT (README.md:399-400): \"`lore audit [--format table|json|md]` - the PRD US-3 coverage + freshness matrix: per registry class, runbook-compiled, check count, real-command count\". The markdown header prints that column as `compiled` (lore/__main__.py:_cmd_audit table).\n\nWHAT SHIPPED (lore/__main__.py:610-634): `is_seen = rb.class_id in seen_classes` (incident presence, from lore/incidents.py), then `row[\"runbook_compiled\"] = is_seen` AND `row[\"incident_seen\"] = is_seen`. The row for a class is only ever built from `compile_all()`, i.e. from a class that HAS a compiled runbook with checks - so the honest value of the documented column is always true for every row, and incident presence is a different fact that landed in the same boolean.\n\nLIVE OBSERVED at HEAD da91c1e (2026-10-23), repo root:\n  $ .venv/bin/lore audit --format json | jq -r '.classes[]|\"\\(.class_id) compiled=\\(.runbook_compiled) checks=\\(.check_count)\"'\n  gateway-drain-window       compiled=true   checks=7\n  shared-checkout-collision  compiled=true   checks=3\n  secret-env-clobber         compiled=true   checks=2\n  disk-pressure-corruption   compiled=true   checks=3\n  cooldown-pin-drift         compiled=false  checks=3      <-- 3 checks printed, \"not compiled\"\n  key-rotation-expiry        compiled=true   checks=2\n  guard-degradation          compiled=true   checks=2\n  spawn-hot-loop             compiled=true   checks=3\n  ingest-backfill-gap        compiled=true   checks=2\n  gateway-guard-violation    compiled=true   checks=2\n  docs-count-drift           compiled=false  checks=2      <-- same shape\n  worktree-reap-data-loss    compiled=false  checks=2      <-- same shape\n  fast-forward-push-reject   compiled=true   checks=2\n  unclassified               compiled=false  checks=0\nA fresh clone on a clean bunker box (df-lore-1023, same HEAD) reports compiled_true=10 / compiled_false=4 with checks_but_uncompiled=3 - the defect travels with the release.\n\nWORSE OUTSIDE THIS REPO (the normal user case): every fleet repo has its own board with its own vocabulary, so `incident_seen` is empty and the whole column reads false. /home/kara/get-h3/shim (430 events, real board) -> incident_seen_count=0, all 14 rows compiled=false. An empty directory -> all 14 compiled=false, while `check_count` still prints 7/3/3/2... The operator-facing table therefore reads \"compiled False, checks 7\", which is self-contradictory, and a reader who trusts it concludes lore ships no runbooks.\n\nTEST SIDE (why CI stayed green): the fix WEAKENED the assertions that used to pin the contract - tests/test_cli_surface.py:85-88 replaced an equality with `assert isinstance(r[\"runbook_compiled\"], bool)` (any bool passes) and :95 accepts `\"coverage_note\" in r or r[\"runbook_compiled\"] is True`; tests/test_lore051_audit_bucket.py:130 merely notes \"runbook_compiled is now computed (not literal True)\". 560 tests pass because nothing asserts the documented meaning.\n\nSEPARATE FROM, and not addressed here: the incident DATA QUALITY (prose matches, window) is LORE-067-R3, and the documentation/skill prose is DOC-8. Do not fold them.","acceptance_criteria":"PASS: with the fix, `uv run python -m lore audit --format json` from (a) the repo root, (b) an empty scratch dir, and (c) a foreign repo with its own .coding-hermes board, prints runbook_compiled=true for EVERY class whose check_count>0 in the same row (live baseline at HEAD da91c1e: 3 rows fail this in the repo root - cooldown-pin-drift/checks=3, docs-count-drift/checks=2, worktree-reap-data-loss/checks=2 - and 14 fail it in an empty dir), while incident presence remains visible in its own `incident_seen` field and `coverage_note` still names the incident source; and tests assert the documented meaning (a test that fails if runbook_compiled is False for any class with check_count>0, replacing `assert isinstance(..., bool)` at tests/test_cli_surface.py:85-88).","acceptance":"PASS: with the fix, `uv run python -m lore audit --format json` from (a) the repo root, (b) an empty scratch dir, and (c) a foreign repo with its own .coding-hermes board, prints runbook_compiled=true for EVERY class whose check_count>0 in the same row (live baseline at HEAD da91c1e: 3 rows fail this in the repo root - cooldown-pin-drift/checks=3, docs-count-drift/checks=2, worktree-reap-data-loss/checks=2 - and 14 fail it in an empty dir), while incident presence remains visible in its own `incident_seen` field and `coverage_note` still names the incident source; and tests assert the documented meaning (a test that fails if runbook_compiled is False for any class with check_count>0, replacing `assert isinstance(..., bool)` at tests/test_cli_surface.py:85-88).","worker_status":"complete","completed_at":"2026-10-23T18:30:00Z","commit_hash":"7bc2804","merge_commit":"7bc2804","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"PENDING_RATE_LIMIT","worker_summary":"Worker commit 2eb651f merged as 7bc2804. Restored runbook_compiled to registry-derived check_count > 0; incident_seen and coverage_note remain separate. Regression assertions added. Gates: 560 pytest passed, ruff check/format clean, count guard PASS. Live audit probes from repo root and empty scratch: zero rows with check_count>0 and runbook_compiled=false. GitReins Tier-2 verdict 24309f1a PASS on evaluated commit 7bc2804. ch:trace row=LORE-067-R2 spec=docs/PRD.md#SC-3 wave=none:serial-fallback test=tests/test_cli_surface.py::test_cli_audit_json_all_classes_honest_freshness doc=none:not-doc-task prompt=/tmp/brief-LORE-067-R2.txt evidence=.gitreins/history/2026-10-23/24309f1a/verdict.json witness=live:audit-json-root+empty-scratch verdict=24309f1a commit=7bc2804 memory=none:not-written"}
