 {"id":"LORE-067-R3","title":"[P3] the incident data path LORE-067 added cannot answer US-3's actual question: a class with incidents but NO runbook is invisible (a novel class_id in events.jsonl yields no row), and any OLD board task that merely NAMES a class id counts as an in-window incident - the 90-day window is not applied to that signal","status":"complete","priority":"P3","created_by":"lore-dogfood-run15","capability_tags":["audit","coverage","incidents"],"complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-10-23T12:22:28.856297+00:00","updated_at":"2026-10-24T06:00:00Z","detail":{},"foreman_note":"Filed by the lore-dogfood lane, tick lore-dogfood-2026-10-23-12-08-40 (run 15), second recurrence of LORE-067. Two independent defects in the same detection path; fix them together because both decide whether `incident_seen` can be trusted. Probes: docs/qa/evidence/run15/novel-class-control-vs-treatment.txt and board-prose-window.txt. The novel-class half is the one that decides whether PRD US-3/SC-2 are deliverable at all.","reasoning":"GAP A - \"classes with incidents but no runbook\" is still unreachable, so the capability LORE-067 was filed to add does not exist yet. Rows are built one per `compile_all()` entry, and the incident scanner's regex is built from the registry's own ids (lore/incidents.py:88-96, `_build_class_pattern(SEED_CLASSES ids)`), so the ONLY class ids that can ever be recognised are ids that already have runbooks. Live probe (fresh fixture dirs, HEAD da91c1e):\n  control  - .coding-hermes/board/events.jsonl with detail {\"class_id\":\"gateway-drain-window\"} (in window)\n             -> rows=14, incident_seen=['gateway-drain-window']          (the mechanism works for KNOWN classes)\n  treatment- same fixture with detail {\"class_id\":\"postgres-deadlock-storm\"} (a class nobody has a runbook for)\n             -> rows=14, incident_seen=[], novel class present in output: 0 (grep -c postgres = 0)\nSo a genuinely new failure class - the fleet's actual reason to build a coverage matrix - is silently dropped. `incident_count()` is computed at lore/__main__.py:611 and immediately discarded (\"side-effect call for future use\"); summary keys are ['classes_with_zero_real_commands','note','stale_classes','total_classes'] - the coverage NUMBER the story asks for is not in the output.\n\nGAP B - the board-task signal is a prose matcher with no window, so it manufactures incidents. lore/incidents.py:141-171 (`_scan_board_task_detail`) joins a task's detail/foreman_note/title and regex-matches class ids; there is no timestamp filter at all (the 90-day cutoff at :203 is applied only to the events file). Live probe: a fixture with ONE generic in-window event (no class_id) plus two tasks dated 2024 whose titles merely say \"docs: mention gateway-drain-window in passing\" and \"rename worktree-reap-data-loss doc heading\" yields incident_seen=['gateway-drain-window','worktree-reap-data-loss'] - two \"incidents\" in the last 90 days from files that record no incident. Control with the two tasks removed: incident_seen=[]. Because runbook_compiled is now incident_seen (LORE-067-R2) the same prose also flips the matrix's headline column, so documentation edits mutate the coverage report.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS FOR US-3/SC-2: PRD US-3 promises \"every failure class seen in the last 90 days\" and SC-2 \"runs on the fleet's last 90 days of incidents\". At HEAD the tool can only report classes it already knows (A) and its notion of \"seen\" includes any old prose mention (B) - so the coverage number is both incomplete and inflated, in opposite directions.","acceptance_criteria":"PASS: `uv run python -m lore audit --format json` in a scratch dir whose .coding-hermes/board/events.jsonl carries one in-window event with detail {\"class_id\":\"postgres-deadlock-storm\",\"action\":\"new\"} reports that class as uncovered (an `uncovered_classes` summary list, or a row carrying class_id=postgres-deadlock-storm with runbook_compiled=false/incident_seen=true), and the summary carries an incident count; AND the same audit in a scratch dir with a generic event and only 2024-dated tasks that merely name class ids reports incident_seen=[] (both controls verified failing at HEAD da91c1e: novel class absent from all output, two 2024 prose mentions counted as incidents).","acceptance":"PASS: `uv run python -m lore audit --format json` in a scratch dir whose .coding-hermes/board/events.jsonl carries one in-window event with detail {\"class_id\":\"postgres-deadlock-storm\",\"action\":\"new\"} reports that class as uncovered (an `uncovered_classes` summary list, or a row carrying class_id=postgres-deadlock-storm with runbook_compiled=false/incident_seen=true), and the summary carries an incident count; AND the same audit in a scratch dir with a generic event and only 2024-dated tasks that merely name class ids reports incident_seen=[] (both controls verified failing at HEAD da91c1e: novel class absent from all output, two 2024 prose mentions counted as incidents).","worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"6457219","merge_commit":"7f53711","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","evidence_run_id":40068168601,"completed_at":"2026-10-24T06:00:00Z","worker_summary":"Worker commit 6457219 merged as 7f53711. lore/incidents.py preserves structured class_id values from in-window events, reports novel classes, and restricts board-task correlation to timestamped structured incident/closure records; lore audit JSON now emits incident_count and uncovered_classes. Acceptance live: novel postgres-deadlock-storm event -> incident_count=1 and uncovered_classes=[postgres-deadlock-storm]; generic event plus 2024 prose-only task -> incident_count=1, uncovered_classes=[], zero incident_seen rows. Focused 39 passed; full 562 passed; ruff check/format, count guard, diff check PASS. GitReins Tier-2 verdict 1b0eda34 PASS. ch:trace row=LORE-067-R3 spec=docs/PRD.md#US-3 wave=lore-foreman-2026-10-24-05-24-47#LORE-067-R3 test=tests/test_lore067_incident_audit.py::test_audit_reports_novel_class_from_windowed_event doc=docs/qa/evidence/run-LORE-067-R3/README.md prompt=/tmp/lore-067-r3-brief.txt evidence=docs/qa/evidence/run-LORE-067-R3/accept-1-novel-class.json witness=live:gh-run-40068168601-success verdict=1b0eda34 commit=7f53711 memory=none:not-written"}
