w, line 105, 5,361 bytes):\n  id, title, status, priority, created_by, reasoning, capability_tags, complexity, created_at, updated_at,\n  detail, fingerprint, foreman_note, acceptance_criteria, acceptance, worker_status, commit_hash,\n  guard_result, ci_result, completed_at, foreman_note, worker_summary, trace\nTwo foreman_note keys. Strict json.loads succeeds (JSON's last-duplicate-wins rule), so the FIRST note - which carries an OPERATOR QUESTION to Bane about the B1-B8 agent-ops tools - is discarded by every reader of the board (boardctl, foremen, dogfood probes), while the second (the tier-2 verdict note) survives. Nothing in the write path refuses it: the bad row was appended, committed and closed.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS beyond the FAIL: (1) the validator's red result stops being a signal - a real future error lands in a board that is already failing, exactly the masking failure mode the dogfood skill names; (2) the append path that produced it is the one lanes use, so the class is live, not historical; (3) record content (an operator question) is silently unreachable - the board is this project's storage-of-record for work items.\n\nSCOPE: do not hand-edit other rows; fix DOC-6's duplicate and add the guard (or the validator repair). Not the same as LORE-068's original 3 errors, which are verified fixed.", "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: `boardctl validate` on .coding-hermes/board/ returns RESULT: PASS (0 errors) \u2014 the DOC-6 row carries exactly ONE foreman_note key and both statements it holds today (the OPERATOR QUESTION note and the GITREINS TIER-2 verdict note) survive a json round-trip; plus a guard so the class cannot recur: the append path (boardctl create/update or the lane's append script) rejects a row whose serialized JSON contains a repeated key, or `boardctl validate` grows an auto-repair for duplicate keys (baseline at HEAD da91c1e: 1 error / 94 warnings, reproduced identically on the pre-append copy).", "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "