-{"id": "PERF-3", "title": "[P3] absorb_sweep reclassifies identical evidence text for every block, reaching 1.993 s at a 600-block repeated trail", "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "created_by": "lore-perf", "reasoning": "Measured one real user-facing path: `lore absorb --window 2h --trail-file docs/qa/evidence/run14c/trail-real.txt`, whose implementation calls `lore.absorb.absorb_sweep()` at `lore/absorb.py:353` and classifies each evidence block at :390-391. The six-line trail is a deterministic real fixture; the harness validates 6 parsed blocks, output semantic equality, and all classified block counts. Python `-O` optimized build, same harness and same input scale for before/after.\n\nBaseline/re-measure command (exact): `hyperfine --warmup 3 --runs 12 'env LORE_PERF_CANDIDATE=0 .venv/bin/python -O /tmp/lore_absorb_perf.py --scale 100 --number 10 --repeats 5' 'env LORE_PERF_CANDIDATE=1 .venv/bin/python -O /tmp/lore_absorb_perf.py --scale 100 --number 10 --repeats 5'` from `/home/kara/get-h3/lore`.\n\nBefore (current code, 600 blocks = 100x six-block fixture): mean 1.993 s \u00b1 0.186 s, range 1.824\u20132.492 s, user 1.879 s, sys 0.113 s, 12 hyperfine runs. Harness internal best batch: 37,832.69 us/op (10 calls x 5 repeats).\nAfter candidate (one change only: memoize `classify(block.detail)` by exact text for the duration of one `absorb_sweep`, preserving first-seen grouping order and output): mean 357.8 ms \u00b1 68.4 ms, range 322.6\u2013554.7 ms, user 288.5 ms, sys 68.9 ms, 12 runs; hyperfine reports 5.57x \u00b1 1.19 faster. Harness internal best batch: 4,274.34 us/op. The candidate output was JSON-semantic-equal to baseline.\n\nScale check with the same harness: duplicate 6-block fixture: baseline 464.96 us/op vs candidate 741.91 us/op at 1x (candidate overhead); 10x: 3,779.22 vs 773.66 us/op (4.88x); 100x: 37,832.69 vs 4,274.34 us/op (8.85x). A unique-text 600-block control narrowed the benefit: baseline 39,067.17 vs candidate 38,544.66 us/op at 100x; therefore this finding is specifically repeated-evidence classification, not a general classifier speedup.\n\nProfile evidence, exact command: `env LORE_PERF_CANDIDATE=0 .venv/bin/python -O /tmp/lore_absorb_perf.py --scale 100 --profile` and same with `LORE_PERF_CANDIDATE=1`. Numeric cProfile ranking before: `absorb.py:353 absorb_sweep` 0.060s total in profile; `classifier.py:190 classify` 600 calls / 0.053s cumulative; 30,000 `re.Pattern.search` calls / 0.032s self; `_keyword_hits` 5,400 calls / 0.011s. Candidate profile: `absorb.py:353` 0.008s; classifier 6 actual calls / 0.001s cumulative, with 600 cache lookups; regex search 894 calls / 0.002s. No flamegraph was warranted: cProfile numerically isolated the regex/classifier hotspot.\n\nProposed one-line implementation direction for foreman: in `absorb_sweep` add a per-invocation dict keyed by exact `block.detail`, classify each distinct detail once, and reuse the Classification for repeated blocks. Preserve no global cache, because unique-text control shows no benefit and a global cache could retain unbounded incident text. Re-measure the exact command above after implementation.\n\nUnverified: candidate was harness-only and not integrated; no production change made; no full pytest/ruff run against a code change; no benchmark of a committed before/after revision; unique-text inputs do not improve; no concurrency or memory-retention measurement.", "capability_tags": ["python", "performance"], "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-10-24T04:22:32.081817+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-28T20:12:05.360446+00:00", "detail": {}, "foreman_note": "Filed by lore-perf tick lore-perf-2026-10-24-04-10-29. Target code was not edited. Candidate is harness-only; foreman must implement the local per-absorb_sweep exact-text classification memo and re-run the exact hyperfine command. Audit event 386 carries the structured evidence.", "worker_status": "dispatched", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "completed_at": null, "worker_summary": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: `grep -n classification_cache lore/absorb.py` exits 0 and prints the per-invocation memo used inside absorb_sweep. PASS: `hyperfine 'env LORE_PERF_CANDIDATE=0 .venv/bin/python -O /tmp/lore_absorb_perf.py' 'env LORE_PERF_CANDIDATE=1 .venv/bin/python -O /tmp/lore_absorb_perf.py'` exits 0 and stdout contains `faster than` plus both benchmark means. PASS: `git diff lore/absorb.py` exits 0 and shows only per-invocation classification memoization in absorb_sweep with no global cache; the benchmark output reports JSON-semantic equality for repeated and unique-text controls.", "acceptance": "PASS: `grep -n classification_cache lore/absorb.py` exits 0 and prints the per-invocation memo used inside absorb_sweep. PASS: `hyperfine 'env LORE_PERF_CANDIDATE=0 .venv/bin/python -O /tmp/lore_absorb_perf.py' 'env LORE_PERF_CANDIDATE=1 .venv/bin/python -O /tmp/lore_absorb_perf.py'` exits 0 and stdout contains `faster than` plus both benchmark means. PASS: `git diff lore/absorb.py` exits 0 and shows only per-invocation classification memoization in absorb_sweep with no global cache; the benchmark output reports JSON-semantic equality for repeated and unique-text controls.", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/lore-PERF-3", "branch": "wt/PERF-3"}
